---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
---

<Base title="isellipsis" description="Find out if an HTML element is currently truncating its text with an ellipsis.">
  <h1>isellipsis</h1>
  <div class="pkg-badges">
    <img alt="npm version" src="https://img.shields.io/npm/v/isellipsis?logo=npm&logoColor=white" />
    <img alt="bundle size" src="https://img.shields.io/bundlephobia/minzip/isellipsis?logo=javascript&logoColor=white" />
    <img alt="license" src="https://img.shields.io/npm/l/isellipsis?logo=open-source-initiative" />
  </div>

  <p>
    Find out if an element is <em>currently</em> truncating its text with an ellipsis (…) - a <code>div</code>, a
    <code>span</code>, an <code>input</code>, a <code>-webkit-line-clamp</code> block, anything. Framework-agnostic
    at its core (<code>isEllipsis()</code>, <code>measureEllipsis()</code>, <code>observeEllipsis()</code>), with a
    React hook and a ready-made <code>&lt;EllipsisTooltip&gt;</code> component in
    <code>@isellipsis/react</code>.
  </p>

  <p>
    The v3 rewrite dropped the old approach of cloning the element and copying every computed style, in favor of
    measuring non-input elements with a <code>Range</code> and inputs with canvas text metrics - both sub-pixel
    accurate, so the old "use integer widths" caveat is gone, and the result is gated on an ellipsis actually being
    painted rather than just "the text is technically too long".
  </p>

  <p>
    <a href="https://github.com/itaym/isEllipsis" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Source</a> ·
    <a href="https://www.npmjs.com/package/isellipsis" target="_blank" rel="noopener">npm</a>
  </p>

  <pre><code>npm i isellipsis
npm i @isellipsis/react</code></pre>

  <p class="section-label">Live playground</p>
  <iframe class="playground-frame" title="isellipsis playground" src="/playgrounds/isellipsis/"></iframe>
</Base>
